3	             Network	          Routing (IP address) or path determination and logical Addressing       Packets 
2	             Data                 Link, MAC address, Frames or physical Addressing                        Frames 
1	             Physical	          Cables, Signals, Media and Binary Transmission                          Bits  

Real-Life Example - (Opening Google) & ( Sending and receiving Letters ) 
Let’s say you type: www.google.com
Layer 7 – Application  - Browser sends HTTP request.
Layer 6 – Presentation - Data gets encrypted using SSL/TLS (HTTPS).
Layer 5 – Session - Session established between client and server.
Layer 4 – Transport - TCP establishes 3-way handshake.
Layer 3 – Network - IP address added for routing.
Layer 2 – Data Link - MAC address added.
Layer 1 – Physical - Bits travel through cable/WiFi.


Comparison of DOD Model with OSI Model and Knowing their Protocols and Devices 
OSI Model              DOD Model               Protocols                                           Devices 
Layer 5,6,7            Application Layer       DNS, DHCP, NTP, SNMP, HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, TELNET      Web server,mail server, Browser and Mailclient
Layer 4                Host to host Layer      TCP, UDP                                            Gateway
Layer 3                Internet                IP, ICMP, IGMP                                      Router, firewall, Switch
Layer 2                Network access          mac, arp,rarp                                       Bridge and layer2 switch
Layer 1                Network access          Ethernet, TokenRing                                 Hub

Summary of the OSI Model: 
1. Physical Layer - To Transmits the bits over the medium, To provide mechanical and electrical Specifications.
2. Data Link Layer - To Organize bits into frames, to provide hop to hop delivery
3. Network Layer - To move packets from source to destination, To provide internet working
4. Transport Layer - To Provide reliable process to process messages delivery and error recovery
5. Session Layer  To establish, manage and terminate the session
6. Presentation Layer - To Translate, encrypt and compress data.
7. Application Layer - To allow access to network resources. 





